Module
  name: game_interface
  description: Create the game interface, where the ingame stuff starts
  author: OTClient team
  website: https://github.com/edubart/otclient
  sandboxed: true
  scripts: [ widgets/uigamemap, widgets/uiitem, widgets/statsbar, gameinterface ]
  # Trimmed for Exp Arena. Brief section 3 has no open world hunting, no loot
  # economy and no trading, so the systems that serve those were dropped from
  # this list: prey, imbuing and its tracker, quest log, VIP list, player trade,
  # bug report, player mount, rule violation, market, unjustified points,
  # paperdolls, stash, highscores, reward wall, forge, tutorial and task board.
  #
  # Names are removed rather than folders deleted. A module that is not in this
  # list is never loaded, `modules.game_X` stays nil, and putting the line back
  # is the entire revert. Several of these also send requests to the server on
  # game start (prey, forge), which a Canary build that does not implement them
  # would have to answer.
  #
  # One exception, and it is the trap in this approach: `autoload: true` beats
  # this list. autoLoadModules picks such a module up whatever is written here,
  # so dropping the name achieves nothing. Of the eighteen above, task board is
  # the only one, and it carries `enabled: false` in its own manifest instead,
  # as game_lootsplitter does. Check that flag before assuming a removed name
  # means a module that is gone.
  load-later:
    - game_walk
    - game_joystick
    - game_shortcuts
    - game_minimap
    - game_healthinfo
    - game_inventory
    - game_mainpanel
    - game_hotkeys
    - game_textmessage
    - game_console
    - game_actionbar
    - game_outfit
    - game_skills
    - game_containers
    - game_battle
    - game_npctrade
    - game_textwindow
    - game_playerdeath
    - game_spelllist
    - game_cooldown
    - game_modaldialog
    - game_shaders
    - game_attachedeffects
    - game_healthcircle
    - game_shop
    - game_notifications
    - game_blessing
    - game_store
    - game_quickloot
    - game_cyclopedia
    - game_creatureinformation
    - game_inspect
    - game_wheel
    - game_proficiency

  @onLoad: init()
  @onUnload: terminate()
